---
// /rental-analysis — intake form redesigned 2026-09-22 per Michael's
// screenshots. Changes from the original build
// (claude/rental-analysis-tool-build.md):
//   - Hero copy rewritten (new H1, lead, benefit-list wording, and a new
//     "No obligation..." footer note under the benefit list).
//   - Form card gained a static header ("Get your personalized rent
//     estimate" + an "About 2 min" time badge) and each step gained a
//     one-line subtext under its heading.
//   - Progress indicator changed from "Step X of Y" + "Z%" to the
//     current step's NAME on the left ("Property address" / "Property
//     details" / "Your information") and "Step X of 3" on the right —
//     no percent text anymore, though the fill bar itself is still
//     percent-width under the hood.
//   - 4 steps collapsed to 3: property type moved into step 1 (with the
//     address), and step 2 dropped the furnished checkbox (not a hard
//     requirement for the estimate — comp-selection.ts defaults
//     furnished false) in favor of four new fields — property status,
//     desired timeline, and current/expected rent — per Michael's
//     screenshots. None of these three feed the estimate logic, only
//     the owner/LeadSimple emails (see validation.ts's header comment).
//     Square footage was also dropped in this pass, then reinstated
//     2026-09-24 (Michael noticed the form never asked for it) — it
//     DOES feed the estimate: comp-selection.ts narrows comps to
//     within +/-20% of subject sqft when both are known.
//   - Address is now three fields (street/city/zip) instead of one
//     freeform address field + an optional unit field; unit is dropped
//     entirely, not carried over.
//   - Name splits into first/last; a "preferred way to connect"
//     dropdown and a real consent checkbox (replacing the old plain
//     consent paragraph) were added to the final step.
//   - Submit button reads "Get My Rental Analysis" on the last step
//     (was "Request My Rental Analysis").
// See db/migrations/0003_rental_analysis_intake_v2.sql and
// validation.ts for the matching backend changes.
//
// The actual <form> (all 3 steps) plus its navigation/validation/
// autocomplete/submit script now lives in
// src/components/RentalAnalysisForm.astro (extracted 2026-09-24) so the
// same real form can also be embedded directly on the homepage and every
// property-management page, instead of those pages only linking here —
// see that component's own header comment for the full reasoning. This
// page keeps its own distinct hero copy (h1/lead/benefit-list below);
// only the form itself moved.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RentalAnalysisForm from '../../components/RentalAnalysisForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free Rental Analysis | Red Door Property Management"
  description="Get a free, data-backed rental estimate for your Indianapolis-area property in minutes."
  path="/rental-analysis"
>
  <section class="section-soft">
    <div class="container analysis-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="section-kicker">Free Rental Analysis</div>
        <h1>What Could Your Indianapolis Property Rent For?</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Start with the property address. We will use the details you provide to prepare a
          local rental estimate and help you understand the next best step for your property.
        </p>
        <ul class="benefit-list">
          <li><span>1</span>Estimated monthly rental range</li>
          <li><span>2</span>Local market and comparable-property context</li>
          <li><span>3</span>Practical recommendations from a local expert</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="lead-note">No obligation and no generic national estimate. Your information is used to prepare your analysis and follow up about the property.</p>
      </div>

      <RentalAnalysisForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
